#X text 20 20 u_map -- the map \, and the only file in Cut It that says what a control means. Devices publish named controls on param \; this turns them into the buses and the output devices' cords \, so nothing in e_ or c_ learns that a nanoKONTROL exists. ref/module/map.md, f 58;
#X text 20 165 creation arg 1: the state directory \, the \$3 u_state takes: the recover breadcrumb lives beside the state files. inlets: none. outlet 1: the Volca \, selector-prefixed -- notes <n> <v> <d> \, cc <c> <v> \, program <n> \, note <n> <v>. outlet 2: the SP-404 \, pad <n> <vel>. One outlet per output device \, wired in u_root (C-2)., f 58;
#X text 700 20 The map is a table \, and mode-dependent: cut-it-map.txt \, one row per mapping \, four atoms always -- <mode> <control> <dest> <arg>., f 76;
#X text 1400 20 The allowlist guard is what makes a table acceptable: a row names a destination that must be a literal argument on the route below \, feeding a handler on this canvas \, and never a send. Skip it and nothing fails., f 76;
#X text 2200 20 A row naming a destination not on the route is a real error \, unknown-dest on err. An unmapped control \, the moses miss below \, is normal and silent on every bus., f 62;
#X text 20 1700 The six mode keys stay hardcoded and come first \, so a mode change never depends on the mode and a broken table cannot strand you. They are the Launchpad's top row \, CC 91-96 \, which g_grid lights as the mode lamps. See the select 0 gates beside them., f 62;
#X text 1080 1700 The divisor: param values are not one unit. Everything is 0-127 except mother's controls \, which are 0-1 \, so all but those are divided by 127 and every handler sees the same 0 to 1 range., f 62;
#X text 2140 1700 C-6: list split emits symbol og-knob-1 \, and route matches a selector \, so without the trim every control would take the reject., f 62;
#X text 20 1930 The reject is the normal path here: almost every control is 0-127. C-8, f 62;
#X text 1080 1930 The value is parked: list split fires its remainder first \, so the value is normalized and waiting in list append's right inlet before the name starts the lookup., f 62;
#X text 2140 1930 The lookup is two atoms wide: text search with a two-atom key matches fields 0 and 1 (item 229) \, so mode-1 og-knob-1 finds that control's row in that mode. A miss \, -1 \, leaves moses' left outlet for the raw row., f 62;
#X text 20 2160 A duplicate mode-and-control pair silently loses: text search returns only the first match. The gate's static lint catches it., f 62;
#X text 1080 2160 Arg then value \, always: unpack fires right to left \, so the value is in a cold inlet or a gate before the arg triggers., f 62;
#X text 2140 2160 Value destinations are c_mapped instances \, and the scaling lives there: tempo is c_mapped bpm 490 10 \, 0-1 over 10 to 500 BPM. Each draws its own row and passes arg and scaled value on only while live. The transport chain holds no state: it reads back r start and r stop., f 62;
#X text 20 2390 The spigot is the trigger test \, the same three boxes everywhere: a press is non-zero after normalizing and a release is 0 \, so one test serves every surface., f 62;
#X text 1080 2390 The Volca handlers build the selector-prefixed message m_volca expects. C-6, f 62;
#X text 2140 2390 volca-prog uses the value as a gate \, since the program number is the arg: a fader release cannot select a patch., f 62;
#X text 20 2620 The table is a file \, not text define -k \, so it diffs by row and edits without Pd. A relative read resolves against the patch folder \, the same on the Mac \, the device and a gate's scratch copy (item 229)., f 62;
#X text 1080 2620 read takes -c first: after the name \, the whole file reads as one line. The read is at loadbang \, undelayed: mother pushes knobs.txt long before 2000 ms \, and a late table dropped the saved tempo (item 234). A missing or empty map should fail a deploy \, and is reported., f 62;
#X text 2140 2620 The mode name is the second atom: the class is u_err's business \, so the key is mode-1. A second r mode \, since receives are free., f 62;
#X text 20 2850 The seed fills a silence and sets no default: nothing else writes mode at load \, and any incoming mode closes the spigot., f 62;
#X text 1080 2850 u_map is a state contributor: mode is an auto key. The table itself is not persisted \, as it is code. The store is fed from the guard's spigot \, not its own r mode \, so a bad mode cannot survive a power cycle \, and by a cord \, because two r mode boxes have no defined order (item 297)., f 62;
#X text 2140 2850 A restore arrives as a real selection: route restore then route mode leaves compose mode-1 with compose as its selector \, the shape s mode wants. It lands at about 3.5 s \, after the seed's spigot has shut., f 62;
#X obj 2820 1160 c_mapped 404-pad%d 127 0;
