#X text 20 4700 Parameter pickup: mother replays knobs.txt at boot \, so the first touch of a knob jumps (443 BPM on knob 1). This holds a control until its value passes through the stored one. Item 236 \, ref/module/map.md, f 62;
#X text 1400 4700 The gate is on the assembled message \, inside c_mapped \, not on the parked value \, which the name would still fire. It sits below the lookup \, so a held knob is still looked up and an unmapped one reports raw., f 62;
#X text 2800 4700 Identity \, then value \, then name: t l l sends the name to the identity route before list split runs \, and list split fires its remainder first \, so the value is decided before the lookup., f 62;
#X text 20 4980 A knob never re-sends its target: m_organelle's change -1 publishes only distinct values \, so a crossing is detected as a side flip \, not as equality., f 62;
#X text 1400 4980 The boot window decides only whether to arm: a first value inside it is a restore \, after it a hand. mother pushes a value either way \, so the knobs.txt probe to the right is the other half (item 239)., f 62;
#X text 2800 4980 Both branches pass the value through \, so a wrong window costs a jump or one sweep \, never silence., f 62;
#X text 20 5260 Per-knob state in two arrays: 0 virgin \, 1 armed with the side unknown \, 2 armed above the target \, 3 armed below \, 4 live. 2 and 3 are the answer they wait for plus two \, so one comparison releases both. Neither array is -k \, so 0 means virgin at load., f 62;
#X text 1400 5260 select 0 1 4's outlet for 4 goes nowhere: live is the absence of work., f 62;
#X text 2800 5260 select -1 keeps every other control out of slot 0: tabread and tabwrite clamp an out-of-range index (Reference \, pure-data). C-8, f 62;
#X text 20 5540 The gate defaults open on every param message \, before the value is read: a broken filter should make a control jump \, not go dead., f 62;
#X text 1400 5540 A mode change does not re-arm: og-knob-1 is tempo in every mode today. Doing it right needs a per-mode memory \, and the arrays would widen from 4 to 24 (ref/module/map.md)., f 62;
#X text 2800 5540 The identity route duplicates the divisor's \, fed by one t a a: a name added to one must go in both., f 62;
#X obj 700 4180 t f f f f;
#X obj 700 4460 t f;
#X text 20 1720 The screen shows the mapped value \, named for the destination (bpm 157 \, volca-cc41 64) \, not the raw position (item 238). volca-key and the button destinations draw nothing (ref/module/map.md)., f 62;
#X obj 3400 3620 loadbang;
